# Cozy Pi 5 — onboard FAN header cooling
#
# The official Pi 5 / case fan plugs into the board 4-pin FAN connector and is
# driven by firmware + kernel thermal trips (NOT Stratux fancontrol).
#
# Stratux fancontrol PWM's BCM GPIO18 (header pin 12) for a discrete GPIO fan.
# Do not use it for the Pi 5 case fan — wrong pin / wrong controller.

# Cooling curve (temperatures in millidegrees C, speed 0–255)
# Slightly earlier than stock defaults for an enclosed avionics case.
dtparam=fan_temp0=40000
dtparam=fan_temp0_hyst=5000
dtparam=fan_temp0_speed=100

dtparam=fan_temp1=50000
dtparam=fan_temp1_hyst=5000
dtparam=fan_temp1_speed=150

dtparam=fan_temp2=60000
dtparam=fan_temp2_hyst=5000
dtparam=fan_temp2_speed=200

dtparam=fan_temp3=67500
dtparam=fan_temp3_hyst=5000
dtparam=fan_temp3_speed=255
